menu "LZ4 Configurations"

    config LZ4_USE_PSRAM
        bool "Prefer PSRAM for LZ4 internal allocations"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default n
        help
            Prefer PSRAM for LZ4's large library-internal heap allocations when
            available. Internal 8-bit RAM is used as a fallback when PSRAM is
            not initialized or cannot satisfy an allocation.

            Allocations of 32 KiB or more (HC workspaces, Frame scratch,
            lz4file buffers) prefer PSRAM. Smaller objects, including Block
            hash tables, prefer internal RAM: compression walks the hash table
            randomly, which is slower in PSRAM.

            Either class falls back to the other region when the preferred
            heap cannot satisfy the request.

    config LZ4_FAST_DEC_LOOP
        bool "Enable LZ4 fast decode loop"
        default n
        help
            Opt into the upstream fast-path decoder. Upstream enables it only
            for x86 and aarch64 builds and leaves it off for other targets
            including Xtensa and RISC-V; this option follows the same
            conservative default for ESP targets.

            Measured on an ESP32-C5 with this component's benchmark
            (compressible input): decompression +17% throughput at a cost of
            about 3 KiB of code size. Enable this option for decompression-
            heavy workloads such as compressed assets, logs, or network
            payloads.

    choice LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE
        prompt "LZ4 Block API hash table size"
        default LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE_16KB
        help
            Memory reserved from the heap by every Block compression state for
            its hash table. Smaller tables shrink the per-call allocation and
            can improve cache locality, at the cost of compression ratio.
            HC and Frame states are not affected.

            Do not place this state on a small FreeRTOS task stack.

        config LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE_1KB
            bool "1 KiB"

        config LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE_2KB
            bool "2 KiB"

        config LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE_4KB
            bool "4 KiB"

        config LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE_8KB
            bool "8 KiB"

        config LZ4_BLOCK_HASH_TABLE_SIZE_16KB
            bool "16 KiB (upstream default)"

    endchoice

endmenu
